 Marks are mounting locations, not cutting instructions.", "Work the example, then use your own project values. Label given, measured, calculated and assumed quantities.", "Show the intended dimensions and a reference edge on your drawing. Another crew member checks before fabrication."], "purpose": "Trades math • measuring and inspection • drawing/plan interpretation", "catchUp": ["Use a larger drawing, fraction strip or teacher-modeled example, then do a fresh measurement and calculation yourself.", "If absent or equipment is unavailable, complete the plan/math practice and arrange the actual practical check. Label unperformed tests pending; do not invent results."]}, "teachingMoment": {"phase": "model", "title": "Plan", "purpose": "Read drawing C: 8 1/2 × 5 1/4-in rectangle; four point centers each 3/4 in from their nearest edges. Marks are mounting locations, not cutting instructions."}, "teachingTool": {"kind": "case-board", "version": 1, "frames": [{"title": "C · Mounting template — mark centers; do not drill", "image": "/trades-etf/template.svg", "alt": "C · Mounting template — mark centers; do not drill. Read drawing C: 8 1/2 × 5 1/4-in rectangle; four point centers each 3/4 in from their nearest edges. Marks are mounting locations, not cutting instructions.", "prompt": "Read drawing C: 8 1/2 × 5 1/4-in rectangle; four point centers each 3/4 in from their nearest edges. Marks are mounting locations, not cutting instructions.", "body": "Read written dimensions; this screen drawing is not to scale. Keep the supplied plan beside your physical work."}]}}, {"id": "mvp-etf-1-06-plan-example", "type": "worked_example", "prompt": "Find the center spacing.", "equation": "Horizontal: 8 1/2 − 2 × 3/4 = 7 in. Vertical: 5 1/4 − 2 × 3/4 = 3 3/4 in.", "work": "Overall dimensions and center spacing are different quantities.", "answer": "Apply the method to your own dimensions or the supplied independent check."}, {"id": "mvp-etf-1-06-make", "type": "prose", "markdown": "Continue the project: build, test, and change a physical feature.", "workshop": {"pageBreakBefore": true, "stage": "Make", "title": "Make the project", "lead": "Continue the project: build, test, and change a physical feature.", "minutes": 45, "notebook": "Record the changed part while you build; retain the earlier version or sketch.", "steps": ["Teacher selects the needed clinic: tape divisions, mixed-number subtraction, or reading views.", "Lay out the full template independently; use only paper marks, not drilling.", "Return to your organizer and apply the practiced skill to a real part. Recheck it after correction."], "purpose": "Trades math • measuring and inspection • drawing/plan interpretation", "catchUp": ["Use a larger drawing, fraction strip or teacher-modeled example, then do a fresh measurement and calculation yourself.", "If absent or equipment is unavailable, complete the plan/math practice and arrange the actual practical check. Label unperformed tests pending; do not invent results."]}, "teachingMoment": {"phase": "investigate", "title": "Make", "purpose": "Continue the project: build, test, and change a physical feature."}, "teachingTool": {"kind": "case-board", "version": 1, "frames": [{"title": "C · Mounting template — mark centers; do not drill", "image": "/trades-etf/template.svg", "alt": "C · Mounting template — mark centers; do not drill. Read drawing C: 8 1/2 × 5 1/4-in rectangle; four point centers each 3/4 in from their nearest edges. Marks are mounting locations, not cutting instructions.", "prompt": "Teacher selects the needed clinic: tape divisions, mixed-number subtraction, or reading views.", "body": "Read written dimensions; this screen drawing is not to scale. Keep the supplied plan beside your physical work."}]}}, {"id": "mvp-etf-1-06-test", "type": "prose", "markdown": "Inspect the work against the plan and the performance requirement.", "workshop": {"pageBreakBefore": true, "stage": "Test", "title": "Test the project", "lead": "Inspect the work against the plan and the performance requirement.", "minutes": 15, "notebook": "Version 1 → test → physical change → comparable retest.", "steps": ["A checker can recover each center from the named datum and written dimensions.", "Retain the first attempt and the correction as evidence of progress."], "purpose": "Trades math • measuring and inspection • drawing/plan interpretation", "catchUp": ["Use a larger drawing, fraction strip or teacher-modeled example, then do a fresh measurement and calculation yourself.", "If absent or equipment is unavailable, complete the plan/math practice and arrange the actual practical check. Label unperformed tests pending; do not invent results."]}, "teachingMoment": {"phase": "discuss", "title": "Test", "purpose": "Inspect the work against the plan and the performance requirement."}, "teachingTool": {"kind": "case-board", "version": 1, "frames": [{"title": "C · Mounting template — mark centers; do not drill", "image": "/trades-etf/template.svg", "alt": "C · Mounting template — mark centers; do not drill. Read drawing C: 8 1/2 × 5 1/4-in rectangle; four point centers each 3/4 in from their nearest edges. Marks are mounting locations, not cutting instructions.", "prompt": "A checker can recover each center from the named datum and written dimensions.", "body": "Read written dimensions; this screen drawing is not to scale. Keep the supplied plan beside your physical work."}]}}, {"id": "mvp-etf-1-06-explain", "type": "prose", "markdown": "Show your own math and plan-reading evidence; have the teacher check your practical work.", "workshop": {"pageBreakBefore": true, "stage": "Explain", "title": "Explain the project", "lead": "Show your own math and plan-reading evidence; have the teacher check your practical work.", "minutes": 10, "notebook": "Individual answer and notebook page; flag any practical check still pending.", "steps": ["If both horizontal edge offsets become 1 in while overall width stays 8 1/2 in, what is the new center spacing? Which two marks move?", "Show your teacher your own measurement/layout and interpreted plan feature. Save one concise response with your calculation, units and notebook page.", "Record a test result and physical revision on paper. Return shared supplies and store the continuing project."], "purpose": "Trades math • measuring and inspection • drawing/plan interpretation", "catchUp": ["Use a larger drawing, fraction strip or teacher-modeled example, then do a fresh measurement and calculation yourself.", "If absent or equipment is unavailable, complete the plan/math practice and arrange the actual practical check. Label unperformed tests pending; do not invent results."]}, "teachingMoment": {"phase": "exit", "title": "Explain", "purpose": "Show your own math and plan-reading evidence; have the teacher check your practical work."}, "teachingTool": {"kind": "case-board", "version": 1, "frames": [{"title": "C · Mounting template — mark centers; do not drill", "image": "/trades-etf/template.svg", "alt": "C · Mounting template — mark centers; do not drill. Read drawing C: 8 1/2 × 5 1/4-in rectangle; four point centers each 3/4 in from their nearest edges. Marks are mounting locations, not cutting instructions.", "prompt": "If both horizontal edge offsets become 1 in while overall width stays 8 1/2 in, what is the new center spacing? Which two marks move?", "body": "Read written dimensions; this screen drawing is not to scale. Keep the supplied plan beside your physical work."}]}}, {"id": "mvp-etf-1-06-evidence", "type": "exit_ticket", "capture": true, "requiredForCompletion": true, "prompt": "If both horizontal edge offsets become 1 in while overall width stays 8 1/2 in, what is the new center spacing? Which two marks move? Include units, enough working to check, and your notebook page/date. Practical evidence is checked with your teacher.", "targetId": "etf26.p1.math", "evidenceRole": "exit", "xp": 10, "workshop": {"taskLabel": "Save your individual evidence", "purpose": "One short response connects your calculation and plan interpretation to the notebook. The teacher observes measuring and building separately."}, "sei": {"visualBlockId": "mvp-etf-1-06-explain", "frames": [{"level": 1, "text": "The plan shows ___. I used ___ to calculate ___. My answer is ___ (units). My notebook page is ___."}, {"level": 2, "text": "My reference is ___. I checked ___ by ___. The test supports ___, with the limit ___."}], "wordBank": ["dimension", "datum", "units", "calculate", "inspect", "revision"], "talkFirst": false}}]}}]$etf_data$::jsonb; begin if (select count(*) from jsonb_array_elements(expected) j join lessons l on l.id=(j->>'id')::uuid where to_jsonb(l) @> j) <> 6 then raise exception 'Stored lesson content does not match authored source'; end if; end $check$;
do $vocab$ declare data jsonb := $etf_data$[{"lesson_id": "5020385b-020f-5887-84d0-e6b591241e8f", "lesson_slug": "mvp-etf-1-01", "name": "ETF P1 · 01 · Build a Stand That Works", "unit_id": "trades-etf-1", "description": "Eight words for this project meeting. Preview three or four at the bench; assign the full set or a selection for review. Practical skills are assessed separately.", "recommended_target_slug": "etf26.p1.vocabulary", "terms": [{"term": "dimension", "tier": 3, "category": "measurement", "definition": "A measured or specified size, such as length, width, or height.", "example": "Label the tray's base length, base width, and wall height as separate dimensions.", "order_index": 0, "difficulty": "easy"}, {"term": "datum", "tier": 3, "category": "measurement", "definition": "A chosen reference point, line, or surface from which measurements are taken.", "example": "Name corner A as the datum and locate three school-zone features from it.", "order_index": 1, "difficulty": "easy"}, {"term": "fraction", "tier": 2, "category": "math", "definition": "A number that expresses parts of a whole; the denominator names the equal parts and the numerator counts them.", "example": "A clearance of 1/8 in on each side adds 2/8 in, or 1/4 in, to a notebook dimension.", "order_index": 2, "difficulty": "easy"}, {"term": "blank", "tier": 3, "category": "fabrication", "definition": "The starting piece of material before it is folded or shaped into the finished part.", "example": "For the model tray, a 5 3/4-in base plus two 3/4-in walls needs a 7 1/4-in blank length.", "order_index": 3, "difficulty": "easy"}, {"term": "NTS", "tier": 3, "category": "drawing", "definition": "Not to scale: a drawing whose written dimensions must be used because its drawn lengths are not proportional to the real sizes.", "example": "Mark your notebook sketch NTS and write the dimensions the builder must follow.", "order_index": 4, "difficulty": "easy"}, {"term": "layout", "tier": 3, "category": "layout", "definition": "The planned or marked positions of parts, edges, and reference lines before making or placing something.", "example": "Lay out the work area's boundaries and fixture locations before placing the paper equipment.", "order_index": 5, "difficulty": "easy"}, {"term": "prototype", "tier": 3, "category": "design", "definition": "A trial version or model used to check a design before committing to a final product.", "example": "Use the paper model to check fit and access before requesting hardware.", "order_index": 6, "difficulty": "easy"}, {"term": "revision", "tier": 2, "category": "communication", "definition": "An identified change to a drawing, plan, or product that replaces an earlier version.", "example": "After checking an unclear endpoint, date the drawing and label the corrected version revision B.", "order_index": 7, "difficulty": "easy"}]}, {"lesson_id": "949c7fc6-a33a-5120-a2a4-6f37f8ae4f43", "lesson_slug": "mvp-etf-1-02", "name": "ETF P1 · 02 · Design for Someone Else", "unit_id": "trades-etf-1", "description": "Eight words for this project meeting. Preview three or four at the bench; assign the full set or a selection for review. Practical skills are assessed separately.", "recommended_target_slug": "etf26.p1.vocabulary", "terms": [{"term": "user need", "tier": 2, "category": "design", "definition": "A practical problem or requirement experienced by the person who will use the result.", "example": "Describe the actual difficulty the school user experiences before suggesting a storage solution.", "order_index": 0, "difficulty": "easy"}, {"term": "clearance", "tier": 3, "category": "layout", "definition": "The space intentionally left between a part and another surface so the part can fit or move.", "example": "Add two 1/8-in clearances to the notebook width to find the tray's inside base width.", "order_index": 1, "difficulty": "easy"}, {"term": "partition", "tier": 3, "category": "layout", "definition": "A dividing part between spaces whose thickness reduces the clear space available.", "example": "Account for two 1/4-in-thick dividers inside the supplied 18-in clear opening.", "order_index": 2, "difficulty": "easy"}, {"term": "inside dimension", "tier": 3, "category": "measurement", "definition": "A distance between the inner faces of a part or opening.", "example": "The model's inside base grows from 5 3/4 × 3 3/4 in to 6 × 4 in.", "order_index": 3, "difficulty": "easy"}, {"term": "outside dimension", "tier": 3, "category": "measurement", "definition": "A distance between the outer faces of a part or assembly.", "example": "The finished tray's outside size includes its wall material; do not confuse it with the flat blank size.", "order_index": 4, "difficulty": "easy"}, {"term": "thickness", "tier": 3, "category": "measurement", "definition": "The distance between the two opposite faces of a material layer or part.", "example": "Include each route's full thickness when locating its top and bottom surfaces.", "order_index": 5, "difficulty": "easy"}, {"term": "prototype", "tier": 3, "category": "design", "definition": "A trial version or model used to check a design before committing to a final product.", "example": "Use the paper model to check fit and access before requesting hardware.", "order_index": 6, "difficulty": "easy"}, {"term": "acceptance criterion", "tier": 3, "category": "inspection", "definition": "A measurable requirement or stated test used to decide whether the work meets the job's needs.", "example": "One criterion is that a partner can locate both divider centers from your drawing without guessing.", "order_index": 7, "difficulty": "easy"}]}, {"lesson_id": "72423444-4bbf-5aa1-834a-a69bd852072c", "lesson_slug": "mvp-etf-1-03", "name": "ETF P1 · 03 · Read the Plan and Cut the Parts", "unit_id": "trades-etf-1", "description": "Eight words for this project meeting. Preview three or four at the bench; assign the full set or a selection for review. Practical skills are assessed separately.", "recommended_target_slug": "etf26.p1.vocabulary", "terms": [{"term": "cut list", "tier": 3, "category": "fabrication", "definition": "A list of the finished pieces to make, with each piece's size and quantity.", "example": "List two 6-ft border pieces and two 4-ft border pieces before deciding how much stock to buy.", "order_index": 0, "difficulty": "easy"}, {"term": "plan view", "tier": 3, "category": "drawing", "definition": "A drawing showing a space or object as viewed from directly above.", "example": "Show the zone boundaries and equipment as seen from above.", "order_index": 1, "difficulty": "easy"}, {"term": "elevation view", "tier": 3, "category": "drawing", "definition": "A drawing looking straight at a vertical face, showing heights and vertical relationships.", "example": "Show the selected divider height in a view of its vertical face.", "order_index": 2, "difficulty": "easy"}, {"term": "stock", "tier": 3, "category": "fabrication", "definition": "Material in the starting size available for making parts.", "example": "Start the cutting plan with one 48-in stock strip.", "order_index": 3, "difficulty": "easy"}, {"term": "area", "tier": 2, "category": "math", "definition": "The amount of a flat surface, measured in square units; a rectangle has area length × width.", "example": "The model 4 × 6 ft display has 24 ft² of surface to cover.", "order_index": 4, "difficulty": "easy"}, {"term": "offcut", "tier": 3, "category": "fabrication", "definition": "A piece left after cutting that may still be usable for another part.", "example": "After four parts and four cuts, a 1/2-in piece of stock remains; decide whether it is useful.", "order_index": 5, "difficulty": "easy"}, {"term": "datum", "tier": 3, "category": "measurement", "definition": "A chosen reference point, line, or surface from which measurements are taken.", "example": "Name corner A as the datum and locate three school-zone features from it.", "order_index": 6, "difficulty": "easy"}, {"term": "verify", "tier": 2, "category": "inspection", "definition": "To check a claim, value, or condition against a measurement, calculation, or other evidence.", "example": "Check the new blank dimensions and test the revised fit before accepting the change.", "order_index": 7, "difficulty": "easy"}]}, {"lesson_id": "84c374fe-da07-5e6f-b298-e0ee6a3c7b08", "lesson_slug": "mvp-etf-1-04", "name": "ETF P1 · 04 · Build Version Two and Check the Cost", "unit_id": "trades-etf-1", "description": "Eight words for this project meeting. Preview three or four at the bench; assign the full set or a selection for review. Practical skills are assessed separately.", "recommended_target_slug": "etf26.p1.vocabulary", "terms": [{"term": "revision", "tier": 2, "category": "communication", "definition": "An identified change to a drawing, plan, or product that replaces an earlier version.", "example": "After checking an unclear endpoint, date the drawing and label the corrected version revision B.", "order_index": 0, "difficulty": "easy"}, {"term": "unit price", "tier": 3, "category": "estimating", "definition": "The price for one stated unit, such as one sheet or one foot of material.", "example": "At the fictional unit price of $4 per panel, each additional panel adds $4.", "order_index": 1, "difficulty": "easy"}, {"term": "quantity", "tier": 2, "category": "estimating", "definition": "The count or measured amount of an item needed or purchased.", "example": "A feasible layout uses four 2 × 3 ft panels to cover the model display.", "order_index": 2, "difficulty": "easy"}, {"term": "total cost", "tier": 2, "category": "estimating", "definition": "The sum of all included costs, with any exclusions stated.", "example": "The classroom comparison is $42 versus $44, excluding tax, delivery, and labor.", "order_index": 3, "difficulty": "easy"}, {"term": "rework", "tier": 3, "category": "fabrication", "definition": "Work done again or corrected because the result did not meet a requirement.", "example": "Correct the dimension that failed, then measure again before marking it accepted.", "order_index": 4, "difficulty": "easy"}, {"term": "fit", "tier": 3, "category": "inspection", "definition": "How well a part matches its intended space and required clearance.", "example": "Place the template in the recess and check the intended gap along every edge.", "order_index": 5, "difficulty": "easy"}, {"term": "thickness", "tier": 3, "category": "measurement", "definition": "The distance between the two opposite faces of a material layer or part.", "example": "Include each route's full thickness when locating its top and bottom surfaces.", "order_index": 6, "difficulty": "easy"}, {"term": "reasonableness check", "tier": 2, "category": "math", "definition": "A quick estimate, comparison, or unit check used to see whether a calculated result makes sense.", "example": "The bay width should be slightly less than 6 in because the partitions occupy some of the 18 in.", "order_index": 7, "difficulty": "easy"}]}, {"lesson_id": "edb5feb9-2032-5469-9fa5-a81247d9c728", "lesson_slug": "mvp-etf-1-05", "name": "ETF P1 · 05 · Hand Over a Product That Fits", "unit_id": "trades-etf-1", "description": "Eight words for this project meeting. Preview three or four at the bench; assign the full set or a selection for review. Practical skills are assessed separately.", "recommended_target_slug": "etf26.p1.vocabulary", "terms": [{"term": "tolerance", "tier": 3, "category": "inspection", "definition": "The allowed variation from a specified dimension or value.", "example": "State the permitted dimensional variation before deciding whether the replacement matches the specification.", "order_index": 0, "difficulty": "easy"}, {"term": "acceptable range", "tier": 2, "category": "inspection", "definition": "The interval of values permitted by the stated limits or tolerance.", "example": "The acceptable interval is 39 3/4 to 40 1/4 in, including the endpoints.", "order_index": 1, "difficulty": "easy"}, {"term": "inspection", "tier": 3, "category": "inspection", "definition": "A deliberate check of the work against its stated requirements.", "example": "Compare the completed model with every acceptance criterion in the plan.", "order_index": 2, "difficulty": "easy"}, {"term": "handover", "tier": 3, "category": "communication", "definition": "The transfer of a completed work package and its essential information to the next person or user.", "example": "Give the next person the brief, drawings, estimate, test record, revisions, and unresolved questions.", "order_index": 3, "difficulty": "easy"}, {"term": "signed difference", "tier": 2, "category": "math", "definition": "A subtraction result that keeps its positive or negative sign; measured minus specified shows the direction of a dimensional error.", "example": "Measured minus specified is 40 3/8 − 40 = +3/8 in, showing the layout is too long.", "order_index": 4, "difficulty": "easy"}, {"term": "traceability", "tier": 3, "category": "communication", "definition": "The ability to follow a result or decision back to its source measurement, calculation, drawing, or test.", "example": "Show which site measurement and calculation support a dimension in the final drawing.", "order_index": 5, "difficulty": "easy"}, {"term": "dimension", "tier": 3, "category": "measurement", "definition": "A measured or specified size, such as length, width, or height.", "example": "Label the tray's base length, base width, and wall height as separate dimensions.", "order_index": 6, "difficulty": "easy"}, {"term": "fit", "tier": 3, "category": "inspection", "definition": "How well a part matches its intended space and required clearance.", "example": "Place the template in the recess and check the intended gap along every edge.", "order_index": 7, "difficulty": "easy"}]}, {"lesson_id": "42f20a3a-960d-556a-a10f-7858a5a1ceaf", "lesson_slug": "mvp-etf-1-06", "name": "ETF P1 · 06 · Workshop: Reproduce a Part from a Plan", "unit_id": "trades-etf-1", "description": "Eight words for this project meeting. Preview three or four at the bench; assign the full set or a selection for review. Practical skills are assessed separately.", "recommended_target_slug": "etf26.p1.vocabulary", "terms": [{"term": "template", "tier": 3, "category": "fabrication", "definition": "A pattern used to transfer a shape or feature locations to another piece of material.", "example": "Make a paper pattern another student can use to reproduce the replacement liner.", "order_index": 0, "difficulty": "easy"}, {"term": "center spacing", "definition": "The distance between the center points or centerlines of two features.", "tier": 3, "category": "project-language", "example": "Two mounting points 3/4 in from opposite edges of an 8 1/2-in plate have 7-in center spacing.", "order_index": 1, "difficulty": "easy"}, {"term": "datum", "tier": 3, "category": "measurement", "definition": "A chosen reference point, line, or surface from which measurements are taken.", "example": "Name corner A as the datum and locate three school-zone features from it.", "order_index": 2, "difficulty": "easy"}, {"term": "offset", "tier": 3, "category": "layout", "definition": "A stated distance and direction from a reference line or point to a feature.", "example": "Locate a fixture 12 in inward from the short end and state the reference edge.", "order_index": 3, "difficulty": "easy"}, {"term": "overall dimension", "tier": 3, "category": "measurement", "definition": "The full distance between the outside endpoints of an object or layout.", "example": "Measure the zone from its first boundary to its last boundary as one overall dimension.", "order_index": 4, "difficulty": "easy"}, {"term": "fraction", "tier": 2, "category": "math", "definition": "A number that expresses parts of a whole; the denominator names the equal parts and the numerator counts them.", "example": "A clearance of 1/8 in on each side adds 2/8 in, or 1/4 in, to a notebook dimension.", "order_index": 5, "difficulty": "easy"}, {"term": "verify", "tier": 2, "category": "inspection", "definition": "To check a claim, value, or condition against a measurement, calculation, or other evidence.", "example": "Check the new blank dimensions and test the revised fit before accepting the change.", "order_index": 6, "difficulty": "easy"}, {"term": "rework", "tier": 3, "category": "fabrication", "definition": "Work done again or corrected because the result did not meet a requirement.", "example": "Correct the dimension that failed, then measure again before marking it accepted.", "order_index": 7, "difficulty": "easy"}]}]$etf_data$::jsonb; item jsonb; saved jsonb; begin for item in select value from jsonb_array_elements(data) loop saved := public.save_lesson_vocabulary((item->>'lesson_id')::uuid,null,item->'terms',false); update public.vocabulary_sets set name=item->>'name',description=item->>'description',created_by='antoccic@fitchburg.k12.ma.us' where id=(saved->>'setId')::uuid; end loop; end $vocab$;
commit; select jsonb_build_object('project',1,'lessons',(select count(*) from lessons where unit_id='trades-etf-1' and not published),'vocabulary_sets',(select count(*) from vocabulary_sets where unit_id='trades-etf-1' and not published),'terms',(select count(*) from vocabulary_terms t join vocabulary_sets s on s.id=t.vocabulary_set_id where s.unit_id='trades-etf-1' and not t.archived));